    "spellcasting": "",
    "biography": {
      "value": "<h2>Salam — Player Character Dossier</h2><p><strong>Level 3 Ranger.</strong> Salam is the quiet, sharpshooting Ranger of the Liberated Toads. Folded from the old Salem file, he is famous for landing a miraculous eye-shot through the Arachnid Matriarch's primary eye cluster during the Battle of the Spider Grove. He also survived the Shadow Estate's rooftop collapse, holding on to Remi's Feather Fall chain during the descent, and has co-led the Toads' perimeter guards.</p><p><strong>Ledger:</strong> 2,220 XP, 10 entries, Level 3, Power 5, Fame 30 Local. The XP ledger remains authoritative.</p><h3>How to play Salam</h3><p>Salam is a sharpshooter with damaged trust. He is quiet and vigilant, woodcarving bows or barricading doors under stress. He excels in ranged combat, elevated positioning, and sensing hidden or undead threats. His inventory contains only actual gear confirmed by the campaign logs.</p><h3>Confirmed inventory</h3><p>Salam carries a light crossbow, a shortbow, a handaxe / woodcarving tools, bolts, arrows, light leather armor, and a torch.</p>",
      "public": "Salam is the quiet sharpshooter of the Liberated Toads. His precision eye-shot on the Matriarch saved Markop, and his forest-ranging senses protect the team from hidden undead."
    }
